{
 "description": "Fit the wild type with its three mutants, signs from receptor biology (description, discarded seeds).\n\nWild-type data alone left C.2's perturbation responses undetermined. With signs from receptor\nbiology they can be represented in the right direction: PDF excitatory (PDFR-1, Galpha-s) turns\npdfr-1's change to -0.21 (`pdf_sign_check.json`), and serotonin's fixed-sign group at its maximum\nwith ser-5 excitatory (Galpha-q, in vivo) gives tph-1 +0.18, passing (`tph1_capacity.json`).\n\n- The model and bounds: V2's (the inhibitory scale at least 0.09, PDF's strengths excitatory), with\n  ser-5's strength held excitatory too.\n- The start: the capacity check's last point, the leave-one-out screen's answer with serotonin's\n  fixed-sign group at 3.0 and ser-5 at +3.\n- The objective: v4's ranking score on the six families plus each of tph-1's, pdfr-1's and\n  tax-4's two lawn differences on its own 64-animal band, each mutant one more family (nine\n  equal families), with both guards.\n- The search: sep-CMA at population 24, sigma0 0.05, 64 animals a candidate, 60 generations on 16\n  workers.\n\nReadouts every 10 generations on the search's mean, on 200 animals (762,000,000 + i). The stop\nrule, fixed before the run: at generation 30, stop if the readout D is more than 1 above its start,\nor if fewer than two mutants pass and their mean |z| has not fallen by at least 1. The branch, fixed\nbefore the run: if at the end the wild type passes at least four families and at least two mutants\npass, the package change and W's design follow; otherwise the result is written up.\n\nSeeds: fit animals 760,000,000 + 64\u00b7k + i; CMA 9486. Run from the repository root.\n",
